{title: 673 - May God Be With You}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #673 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 673}
{meta: category Sentences and Responses - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]May God be [Bb7]with [Eb]you [Bb]Till we [Eb]meet a[Bb]gain,
[Bb7]May [Gm7]God [Fm7]be[Gm]with [Bb7]you, [Eb]Keep [Ab]you [Bbsus]safe[Fm]till [Eb]then;
[Eb]And [Gm7]may His [C]bless[C7]ings [Fm]Be within [Eb]your [Fm]heart,
[Eb]May God [Cmaj7]be[Gm]with [Cm]you [Ab]While we’re [Ab7]a [Fm]part,
[Eb]May [Fm]God [Cm]be [Bbsus]with[Bb7][Ebsus]you.[Eb]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]May [Bb7]God be [Eb]with [Bb]you, Watch [Eb]you [Bb]from above,
[Bb7][Gm7]May [Fm7]God [Gm]protect [Bb7]you [Eb][Ab]in [Bbsus]His [Fm]tender [Eb]love;
[Eb]And [Gm7]with [C]the [C7]dawning Of [Fm]each [Eb]bright, [Fm]new day,
[Eb]May [Cmaj7]God [Gm]be [Cm]with you, [Ab]To [Ab7]guide [Fm]your way,
[Eb][Fm]May [Cm]God [Bbsus][Bb7]be [Ebsus]with [Eb]you.
{end_of_verse}
